{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And the she-ass saw me and swerved before me.</b> That is to say: she was before me the whole time; only, she swerved to the right or to the left." "<b>Perhaps she swerved מפני.</b> But if she swerved מפני altogether, in that she was turning backward because of the pressure that she was suffering — then you I would have killed, because you were pressing her. <b>מפני</b> — aside from facing." "<b>And her I kept alive.</b> For she was coerced. And so it is, that there is a distinction between לפני and מפני, for מפני means 'aside from the sight of the face,' as in ונשל הגויים האלה מפניך, 'He will dispossess these nations מפניך' — מורישם מפניך." "<b>Also you I would have killed.</b> Rashi: this is an inverted verse, etc. That is to say: if I were to expound it as it is written, it would turn out that וגם attached to אותכה would be extending something in the category of אותך — that is, a person with you. But now, when you expound it after the inversion: גם הרגתי אותך — to include something in the category of killing, which is the delay, as Rashi explained. Another interpretation: <b>גם</b> — to include the killing along with the pressing. And some interpret the words as written: <b>Also you I would have killed</b> — to include the servants who went with me, who did not swerve from the road; and therefore Scripture does not mention them from here onward; also you, with a kaf." "<b>[</b> Variant reading: <b>Also you I would have killed.</b> Rashi: this is an inverted verse. That is to say: if I were to expound it as it is written, it would turn out that גם is attached to אותך, and I would be extending something in the category of אותך, which is the animal. And this is what it says: 'Perhaps she swerved מפני — then by now גם אותך ואותה החייתי.' But now that she swerved מפני — אותך, ואותה החייתי. And not so, for she was killed because of the dignity of creatures; therefore one must expound it inverted, according to Rashi's interpretation. (16) <b>]</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {4 "The bracketed passage and the parenthetical '16' appear to be a textual variant or marginal note from a different witness, here rendered as found."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:26.608350769Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}